Translation patch: libsignal_core::curve::PublicKey::serialize

Change: the function returns `Box::from(result)` instead of `result.into_boxed_slice()`.
Why: Aeneas's Lean standard library models `From<Vec<T>> for Box<[T]>` (`alloc.vec.FromBoxSliceVec.from`), but not `Vec::into_boxed_slice`. The extraction therefore declares `alloc.vec.Vec.into_boxed_slice` as an axiom.
Behaviour: same values. At the pinned rustc, `impl From<Vec<T, A>> for Box<[T], A>` is `fn from(v) -> Self { v.into_boxed_slice() }` (library/alloc/src/vec/mod.rs).

diff --git a/rust/core/src/curve.rs b/rust/core/src/curve.rs
--- a/rust/core/src/curve.rs
+++ b/rust/core/src/curve.rs
@@ -128,7 +128,7 @@ impl PublicKey {
         match &self.key {
             PublicKeyData::DjbPublicKey(v) => result.extend_from_slice(v),
         }
-        result.into_boxed_slice()
+        Box::from(result)
     }

     pub fn verify_signature(&self, message: &[u8], signature: &[u8]) -> bool {
